.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt RIPEMD160_INIT 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm RIPEMD160 ,
.Nm RIPEMD160_Init ,
.Nm RIPEMD160_Update ,
.Nm RIPEMD160_Final
.Nd RIPEMD-160 hash function
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/ripemd.h
The following functions have been deprecated since OpenSSL 3.0, and can
be hidden entirely by defining
.Ar OPENSSL_API_COMPAT
with a suitable version value, see
.Xr openssl_user_macros 7 :
.Ft unsigned char *
.Fo RIPEMD160
.Fa "const unsigned char *d"
.Fa "unsigned long n"
.Fa "unsigned char *md"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo RIPEMD160_Init
.Fa "RIPEMD160_CTX *c"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo RIPEMD160_Update
.Fa "RIPEMD160_CTX *c"
.Fa "const void *data"
.Fa "unsigned long len"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo RIPEMD160_Final
.Fa "unsigned char *md"
.Fa "RIPEMD160_CTX *c"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
All of the functions described on this page are deprecated.
Applications should instead use
.Xr EVP_DigestInit_ex 3 ,
.Xr EVP_DigestUpdate 3
and
.Xr EVP_DigestFinal_ex 3 .
.Pp
RIPEMD-160 is a cryptographic hash function with a 160 bit output.
.Pp
.Fn RIPEMD160
computes the RIPEMD-160 message digest of the
.Fa n
bytes at
.Fa d
and places it in
.Fa md
(which must have space for RIPEMD160_DIGEST_LENGTH == 20 bytes of
output).
If
.Fa md
is NULL, the digest is placed in a static array.
.Pp
The following functions may be used if the message is not completely
stored in memory:
.Pp
.Fn RIPEMD160_Init
initializes a
.Vt RIPEMD160_CTX
structure.
.Pp
.Fn RIPEMD160_Update
can be called repeatedly with chunks of the message to be hashed
.Pf ( Fa len
bytes at
.Fa data Ns ).
.Pp
.Fn RIPEMD160_Final
places the message digest in
.Fa md ,
which must have space for RIPEMD160_DIGEST_LENGTH == 20 bytes of output,
and erases the
.Vt RIPEMD160_CTX .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn RIPEMD160
returns a pointer to the hash value.
.Pp
.Fn RIPEMD160_Init ,
.Fn RIPEMD160_Update
and
.Fn RIPEMD160_Final
return 1 for success, 0 otherwise.
.Sh NOTE
Applications should use the higher level functions
.Xr EVP_DigestInit 3
etc.
instead of calling these functions directly.
.Sh CONFORMING TO
ISO/IEC 10118-3:2016 Dedicated Hash-Function 1 (RIPEMD-160).
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr EVP_DigestInit 3
.Sh HISTORY
All of these functions were deprecated in OpenSSL 3.0.
